  I've recently seen a few requests for cheet sheats. I've still got the
Hack Tutorial, which I think is still the most complete such document. It's
current up through NetHack 2.2, but not 2.3 (no stooges, gremlins, sinks,
or sacrifices).

  Altogether, it's about 93k in length, and I send it out in three smaller
files with instructions for re-assembling it. There's also a small file of
fixes that Ken Arromdee posted after the last time the tutorial went around.
I haven't put these fixes in, though; you'll have to do that yourself.

  If you're interested, send me a request. If I get more than a few requests,
I'll post it to the net, mainly because I'm a lazy person, but also because I
often have a hard time finding paths to people.

  Would someone else like to become the keeper of the tutorial? I don't play
Hack anymore (although I'm waiting for 3.0), so I don't have much interest
in it. Someone would have to edit in the changes that I have in the extra file,
and the changes for version 2.3 and future versions. I also will be leaving
this site soon, to go back to school, so I won't have the time to mess around
with it, or the space for the files.

  Please, someone take this thing off my hands, or it may vanish forever!
